FEX on Android: FEXServer serves on its abstract socket alone when its filesystem socket's path
does not fit sun_path.

FEXServer makes an abstract socket and a filesystem socket in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. Below a long
Android data folder (adopted storage: /mnt/expand/<uuid>/user/<n>/<package>) that path, and the
<uid>.FEXServer.Socket fallback in the same folder, exceed the 108 bytes of sun_path, and
tcp_acceptor::create ends the process on a name that long. The filesystem socket is then skipped
and the server keeps its abstract socket, which clients try first. Steam builds are unchanged.

 Source/Tools/FEXServer/Main.cpp        | 6 ++++++
 Source/Tools/FEXServer/ProcessPipe.cpp | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/FEXServer/Main.cpp b/Source/Tools/FEXServer/Main.cpp
index 86345a6..3409748 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/FEXServer/Main.cpp
+++ b/Source/Tools/FEXServer/Main.cpp
@@ -191,9 +191,15 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv, char** const envp) {
 #endif
 
   if (!ProcessPipe::InitializeServerSocket(false)) {
+#ifndef FEX_STEAM_SUPPORT
+    // The abstract socket above serves: clients try it first. A socket path that does not fit
+    // sun_path (an Android app's runtime folder below a long data folder) does not stop the server.
+    LogMan::Msg::IFmt("[FEXServer] No filesystem socket; serving on the abstract socket only");
+#else
     // Couldn't create server socket for some reason
     PipeScanner::ClosePipes();
     return -1;
+#endif
   }
 
   // Switch this process over to a new session id
